{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "issue": 28,
  "purpose": "Current PB and lifetime PB selection over sets + manual entries. Current = best record after the reset line (when set) AND fresh. After the line is calendar-day exclusive (`achievedAt > resetAt`). When the calendar days are equal, a same-day timestamp tie-break applies: record.occurredAt (created_at) > resetOccurredAt (exercise_resets.updated_at) counts as after the line; missing timestamps keep equal-day excluded (OQ-D2 / TC-D7). Timestamps are never used when the calendar days differ, and never used in staleness/period math or equal-value latest-wins. Lifetime = best record overall — no reset filter, no freshness filter. Undated manuals (achievedAt null) are NEVER fresh — regardless of the staleness setting — so they are lifetime-only; current is a claim about now, which an undated entry cannot support even when time-filtering is off. Reset does not affect undated records for lifetime.",
  "openQuestions": [
    {
      "id": "OQ-D2",
      "topic": "achievedAt equal to resetAt (current only)",
      "question": "For current PB, achievedAt == resetAt is NOT after the line (strictly after). Confirmed decision.",
      "proposedDefault": "strictly after; equal is excluded from current"
    }
  ],
